** Session 6: A Disquieting Dilemma **



   I don't figure that I can safely kill Renrut yet, so I need some
cash...

   I sell off a whole bunch of garbage (mostly; armor and weapons,
that I figure aren't magical) to Possogroenoe. I'll get all my money
back from him, later on in the game, any way (when I'm chosen to steal
souls for the glory of Anhur).

   Next; I buy the brass lantern from Izchak, and the stehtescope from
Renrut.

   Let's see what the levels below Temple Town look like, in the
Caverns...

   The stehtescope sure made things easier! <nod head>

   Dagger chucking was going much, much, better now too. <nod head
twice>

   I was able to practice with an elven broadsword, and a hilted
polearm. Both the broadsword, and polearm, boxes were soon available
to be checked - when, and if, I should want to. I'm fully planning on
eventually acquiring; the runesword "Stormbringer", and a spetum
(forked polearm), this game. May as well get the practicing done now.
I always like the levels below Temple Town for these practice
sessions. The gnomes and dwarves are easy at this point - for my
characters.
 
   Just got down the stairs to level 8 when...

<You kill the baby corocodile! Welcome to experience level 9. >

Elryk the Thaumaturge  St:8 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:9 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:8  $:0  HP:72(72)  Pw:98(98)  AC:-2  Exp:9  T:5088

   Hey! Look at that. My strength has gone up a point, somewhere.
<laugh!>

   Later on...

< You step into a polymorph trap. You feel momentarily different. >

T:5321

   Okay. That was odd. In fact, it was downright strange... 

   I looked at all my different screens. I couldn't see anything that
had changed (?). Like; I didn't even have my ring of polymorph control
on! Any way, that's the first time that a polymorph trap has not
functioned, in the usual manner, when I've stepped on one. Maybe I
made my saving throw...? Am I polymorph resistant, somehow...?

   There's always something new that happens to me in this game
(Nethack), or like here; that doesn't function the same.

   Any way: Lucky me again! <pat head>

   This was for three big reasons...

   #1: I hate stepping into these things. They're usually a good way
to lose some pieces of armor.

   #2. You never know what you'll turn into. (Mimics are blind, so you
can't see what's around you, and it's easy to starve to death.
Cockatrices can't carry anything heavier than lock picks. Bats are a
joke when trying to fight anything. Quivering blobs take - absolutely
- forever to get anywhere. That's just naming a few...) <roll eyes>

   #3: That was a good reminder. Now I have my ring of polymorph
control on my finger when exploring unknown areas - just in case...

   Just got to Caverns level 10. I see a velvet spellbook. 

   Woah! First chance at maybe getting a new spell! I take a step
towards it...

< You sense a faint wave of psychic energy. >

T:5741

   I freeze at the keyboard.

   Oh no... 

   That's the most despicable creature there is in this game! Well, at
least, that I'm aware of. I shudder at the prospect of ever being
bushwhacked by one again...

   My mind says: Turn back! Everything is going too good this game. No
use taking chances now. What if I fall in a pit or something. Then
this thing can... <cringe + shudder> ... I don't want to even think
about it!

   But: I also want that spellbook! I'm a wizard. These things are
what I depend on to get new spells. Spells are a vital part of my
arsenal to accomplish my goals...

   <big huge dilemma>

   I ponder...

   <shake head>

   Okay. I'm going to try and get it...

   My eyes are constantly flicking between the main screen, and the
message area - for each and every single click on the clock!

   Even though I'm an elf; I'm searching ("s") two times, for every
step, out of a square, that I take.

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   Those are the thoughts - THAT I FORCE - into my head constantly, as
I slowly advance towards that spellbook...

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

    Almost there. No sign of the creature yet. Then the thought hits
me...

    Oh my goodness!! I nearly forgot: Sometimes they're invisible!!!

    I put on my ring of see invisible. Now I move the look (";") all
over the screen. Okay. Looks clear. Start moving again...

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   I got it!

   Now; I retrace my steps back to the stairs. I make sure that I step
- on exactly the same squares - that I took to this one...

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   "No chances." "Can't be too cautious." "There is no need to rush
anything."

   I'm back upstairs. <hang head + two big thumbs up!>

   I'm heading back to Temple Town...

   Later on, I killed an owl bear that had a wonder whistle on him.
Man; what luck I'm having this game. <smile>

T:5915

   Back at the base camp in Temple Town. 

   Had my loot appraised at Possogroenoe's General Store. I'll have to
keep him alive for a while. It's handy to be able to do everything at
just one shop.

   I make a note: "Make sure not to kill Possogroenoe; unless there is
another general store in the Mazes of Menace or - until I get a
spellbook of Identify."

   Bonus discoveries: I think I found a +1 axe, and a +1 shortsword,
amongst my booty. The velvet spellbook wasn't cursed.

   Read the velvet spellbook...

< You begin to memorize the runes. You add the "remove curse" spell to
your repertoire. >

T:6205

   Now I have three spells I can use (The last one work's better if; I
don't wear the shield, and I do wear the robe.). And this new spell is
a handy one!

   Save game. Several important things were accomplished this session.
I'm very satisfied. <smile>

